<!--
This file is the working pointer for Claude Code's devkit pack. It changes
constantly during feature work and is cleared at `/feature-merge`.

Field meanings:
  Active feature  short slug matching docs/specs/<slug>.md, or "none"
  Active branch   current git branch, or "main" when idle
  Phase           one of: idle | spec-draft | spec-approved | plan-draft |
                  plan-approved | building | checkpoint | merging | in-review
  Spec / Plan     paths to the active spec and plan, or "—" when idle
  PR              URL or owner/repo#N while Phase is in-review; "—" otherwise.
                  Set by /feature-merge when it opens the PR; cleared at
                  closeout once the PR has merged.
  Gated baseline  the last commit SHA that passed gates 1-3. Set when the PR
                  opens and after every successful gate rerun. /feature-merge
                  compares it against the PR tip to decide whether a rerun
                  needs the gates -- comparing local vs remote tips cannot
                  work, because /pr-review pushes its fixes and makes them
                  agree.
  Next step       short pointer to the next plan step when phase = building

The Open questions section captures things deferred mid-feature that need
the user's input. /checkpoint reads and helps resolve these.

During Phase: in-review it holds review findings accepted for THIS
feature and not yet fixed. It is cleared at /feature-merge, so anything
deferred PAST this feature must go to the findings ledger instead --
/pr-review routes cross-feature deferrals there as REV rows. Parking a
durable finding here discards it at merge.

Already-answered review threads are NOT tracked here; the forge itself is
that ledger (a reply carrying the pack's marker means handled).

The Parked features section tracks features whose branch exists but whose
active state has been cleared so a different feature can run. The
canonical way to park is `/checkpoint park` (slice 4) — the documenter
skill proposes the state.md edit and the Parked-features entry.
Manually: (a) reset Active feature to none and Phase to idle, (b) append
one line under "Parked features" naming the branch and what was last
completed. Resume by checking out the branch and re-populating the top
fields.
